In this section, we aim to examine whether the introduction of the \textbf{LH}-plugin affects the scalability of the original models.
We compare the impact of different training data sizes on accuracy. Specifically, we sample 20\%, 40\%, 60\%, 80\%, and 100\% from the Chengdu dataset (TDrive for \textbf{ST2Vec}) to train different trajectory similarity models. The results, as depicted in Figure \ref{fig:scala}, lead us to conclude: 

\noindent(1) With an increase in training data, there is a significant improvement in trajectory similarity accuracy across different models. 

\noindent(2) The inclusion of the \textbf{LH}-plugin results in noticeable enhancements in accuracy across all data sizes, with the accuracy curves before and after adding the \textbf{LH}-plugin exhibiting similar shapes. Thus, it can be concluded that the \textbf{LH}-plugin can significantly improve the accuracy of trajectory similarity models regardless of the training data size.


