At the same time,
using standard methods
in model checking \cite{GradelOtto}, 
it is straightforward 
to verify that model checking can be performed in PTIME if the whole model
is given \emph{explicitly} as input, 
including the set of possible states
and the comparative similarity
relations. However, explicit models  may be extremely large
and so unpractical. 

