\subsubsection{Service Plan}
Starlink recommends the Standard service plan for households and the Priority plan for businesses and high-demand users. However, neither of these plans supports mobility. In contrast, the Mobile plan allows roaming, enabling users to move terminals between locations, making it suitable for RVs, nomads, and campers. The Mobile Priority (mobility) plan provides in-motion connectivity for both land vehicles and vessels at sea. This plan is particularly suited for maritime operations, emergency response, and mobile businesses. In this paper, the terminal is subscribed to a Mobile Priority (mobility) service plan.

