% \subsection{Implementation}
We utilize the annealing data quality assessment approach widely used in other studies \cite{blakeney2406does,grattafiori2024llama}. We continue pre-train the Mistral-7B-v0.3\footnote{https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.3} model for 8,000 steps (30B Tokens), applying a learning rate schedule that annealed from 3e-5 to 3e-6. We keep some learning rate bandwidth for instruction fine-tuning using ShareGPT data to prepare the model for benchmarking. For all our experiments, we construct a dataset comprising 25\% conversational data, 5\% Project Gutenberg books\footnote{Books data in the RedPajama dataset was replaced with Project Gutenberg content due to copyright concerns.}, and 70\%  RedPajama v1\footnote{Content from sites listed in the U.S. Notorious Markets for Counterfeiting and Piracy report were excluded.} Web content. Following this data composition, we prepare four variations to study our proposed solution in practice. 

