\section{conclusions}

NEC proves to be extremely efficient by calculating optimal or near optimal vertex cover on known benchmark graphs. Its worst case has a selection ratio of 1.5[7].
It is experimentally observed to be fast (as compared to current algorithms such as COVER) while the candidate node selection makes sure that it selects high valued candidates. One area left to explore is the impact of graph density and selection ratio and should be taken up in future studies.


