The data set with the lowest mean and standard deviation KL divergence between the data's histogram and the Gaussian distribution should likely have the best Gaussian approximation. Surprisingly, the data set with the poorest Gaussian SDR for voltage magnitude (refer to Table \ref{tb:sdr_euro}), the LV semi-urban data set, has the lowest mean and standard deviation KL divergence. The MV two substation data set has the highest mean and standard deviation KL divergence from the Gaussian approximation of its distribution. The MV two substation data set has the joint highest SDR at 94.7\% (along with the MV ring data set). These results suggest the KL divergence mean and standard deviation are poor metrics when used alone to predict the Gaussian based algorithm performance of a realistic network model.   

