Focusing on semantics and compiler verification, we have not invested any effort to optimize or streamline the software proof flow.
Nevertheless, for all programs we have proven constant-time using any of our semantics, the time and code required to prove the actual constant-time property is a small fraction (around 10\%) of proving memory safety and defined behavior.
