    $Y^{p}$. 
    %
    \begin{align*}
        P(L^{p}&=1  \mid x^{p}, i) 
            = \int\limits_{\mathcal{X}}
            P(L^{p}=1  \mid x^{p}, x, i) p(x  \mid x^{p}, i)\D x\\
