         Case & State of processor $(I,J)$ \\
         \hline
         1 & Contains a block to be zeroed out -- will (approximately) diagonalize a $2b \times 2b$ matrix if $I < J$.\\
         2 & Lies on the diagonal of the processor grid and to the left of a superdiagonal block being zeroed out (will broadcast pieces of the corresponding rotation matrix to block row/column $I$).\\
         3 & Lies on the diagonal of the grid and below a superdiagonal block being zeroed out (will broadcast pieces of the corresponding rotation matrix to block row/column $J$).\\
         4 & Will apply a rotation on the right, exchange blocks with a rightward processor in the same row. \\
         5 & Will apply a rotation on the right, exchange blocks with a leftward processor in the same row.\\
         6 & Will apply a rotation on the left, exchange blocks with a lower processor in the same column. \\
         7 & Will apply a rotation on the left, exchange blocks with an upper processor in the same column.\\
    \end{tabular}
\end{table}
