We see that a reasonable variable heuristic makes a difference as \texttt{FMplex-a-Rand-*} perform much worse than \texttt{FMplex-a-MFO} and \texttt{FMplex-a-MCL}.
However, between the latter two, there is no significant difference.
While our first optimization used in \texttt{FMplex-b-MFO} has no big impact, the backtracking implemented in \texttt{FMplex-c-MFO} allows for solving more instances within the given resource limits.

