with $T>R>P>S,$ and classically, T is the temptation to defect, R the reward for mutual cooperation, P the punishment for defection, and S the so-called "sucker"'s payoff to the player who defects while the other cooperates.

\item \textcolor{blue}{Matching Pennies}: This models zero-sum games with no pure Nash Equilibrium, with the typicall payoff
