      & \multicolumn{1}{c}{} & \multicolumn{2}{c}{Husband}\\
      & \multicolumn{1}{c}{} & \multicolumn{1}{c}{$O$}  & \multicolumn{1}{c}{$F$} \\\cline{3-4}
      \multirow{2}*{Wife}  & $O$ & $(3,2)$ & $(0,0)$ \\\cline{3-4}
      & $F$ & $(0,0)$ & $(2,3)$ \\\cline{3-4}
    \end{tabular}
  \end{table}

We then proceed with solving the game. 

\begin{enumerate}
\item This game has clearly two pure Nash Equilibria at $(F,F)$ and $(O,O).$ This prompts the need to randomize.
\item We look for a mixed Nash Equilibrium: The Wife chooses Football  with probability $p$ and the husband with probability $q.,$ leading to the updated mixed matrix

