\end{eqnarray}
with $\nu \in \Q_{<0}$ and $h(z)=1+z^{-\frac{\nu}{\ellmahl-1}}$ is represented in Figure \ref{fig:Newt bis}.

This operator has two slopes, namely  
$$
\mu_{1}=0 < \mu_{2}=-\frac{\nu}{(\ellmahl-1)\ellmahl},
$$ 
with multiplicities $r_{1}=r_{2}=1$.
\end{example}



