Mini-Splatting with \revised{the new renderer}{StopThePop rendering} initially decreases image quality as the ordering of Gaussians diverges from the learned ordering, causing vastly different per-pixel RGB colors and a significant drop in image quality (${\sim} 1.5$ dB). 
