%Istvan--this is clear, thank you.

The realization that LLMs need to be integrated with specialized tools is gaining traction in M\&S research~\shortcite{ZHANG2024114788} and echoes a broader interest in positioning LLMs as middleware instead of the sole solution~\shortcite{lehmann2024towards,calvetcan}. In this paper, our main contribution is to address the two core questions raised by the opportunities and challenges of integrating LLMs with specialized tools to accomplish modeling and simulation tasks:
\begin{itemize}
    \item[\textbf{Q1}] If the LLM is to act as a translator, then which \textit{language} should it translate into and which \textit{tool} should it call depending on the M\&S task? 
    \item[\textbf{Q2}] Which software \textit{architecture} could efficiently integrate LLM as a middleware to support the interoperability of specialized M\&S tools without creating performance bottlenecks?
    %\id{RAGs and sorts are missing here, and some advanced LLM techniques. I'll add these in the later sections.}
