\paragraph{Invocation Exit.}
(\verb|lines 8-16|) Transitions of this type leave invocations, formally defined by the set $\mathit{Exit}(G) = \{\transition{r}{a,\alpha/\beta}{s} \in \delta \mid r \in G_Q \land s \notin G_Q\}$.
