\begin{figure}[h]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=85mm,scale=0.5]{merged2.jpg}
\caption{Financial data}
\end{figure}




\bigskip

\textbf{Insights into personal energy data} (DSF2) 
Users are provided with real-time and historic information on their electricity production (green) and demand (blue). A time series graph is accompanied by summary key performance indices (KPIs) on production, demand, ratio, self-consumption and self-sufficiency ratio. Both, the graph and the KPIs are interactive on mouse-overs and update with the adjustment of the timeframe. Users can choose timeframes at given intervals (buttons on the left side), with a calendar feature (right) or a zoom band (below). 



\bigskip
\textbf{Insights into financial data} (DSF3) 
Quartierstrom furthermore provides users with insights into their finance situation related to selling own electricity and covering demand by buying from the neighborhood or the grid. Revenue is in green, costs in blue and the financial benefit of Quartierstrom in pink. Again, users can adjust the timeframe considered according to their preferences. 

\bigskip
\textbf{Insights into community-level energy data} (DSF4) 
The webapp further provides users with insights on energy data at the community level. This allows users to estimate their own contribution and to derive whether the community is self-sufficient or needs to buy electricity from the grid to cover its demand.  

%\begin{figure}[h]
%\includegraphics[width=85mm,scale=0.5]{merged3.jpg}
%\caption{Community-level energy data}
%\end{figure}


The webapp is currently being tested in the field with 37 households. First tracking data indicates that almost all participating households actually opened an account and most of them log in quite frequently to either retrieve insights into their data or to adjust price limits. In addition to the webapp, participants receive monthly reports by email to inform them and to remind them of the ongoing project. More insights will be available in the course of the project.


\section{Conclusion and outlook}

The present article introduces the conceptual idea behind the Quartierstrom project as well as some details on the implementation. Most of the conceptualization, development and implementation in the field has been tackled throughout 2018. The developed blockchain platform with integrated double auction application and its user interface has been launched in January 2019 and is now operational for one calendar year. Within this period consumption, production and trading data will be collected and analysed. The quantitative data collection is accompanied with surveys and interviews of participants to gain insights about user preference and general acceptance of the system. 
\\ \\
As of the second half of the calendar year 2019, battery systems will be integrated to optimize the energy flows at the community level rather than on the household level. Controlling batteries at the community level shall demonstrate an increase in self-consumption and self-sufficiency of the entire community and provide a more effective way to integrate costly batteries.


